cd /home/joaquin/work/FA && python3 tools/plan.py design kit_benchmark \
 --question "Fair NLO D-scan (step 3, Bakar's protocol): on KIT's e+e- -> t t~ one-loop virtual, with D = 1e2, 3.2e2, 1e3, 3.2e3, 1e4 bulk target points, does a model fine-tuned from the fair_nlo parent (runs/kit/kit_pretrain_fair_nlo, FA-ccin2p3-03ea3719: every catalog_v4 tree incl. e+e- -> t t~ LO, 10 one-loop pools bulk only, the t t~ family's one-loop held out) beat Bakar's baseline, a from-scratch V/B with the exact Born, on KIT's bulk_test and every hard bin? Both arms learn V/B (data.target_over_born, the exact Born from KIT's file for the same events) so the only difference is pretraining. Feeds the KIT report's fair NLO table and whether pretraining saves one-loop data on KIT's setup as it did on the catalog (pretrain_data_saving)." \
 --prior "pretrain_data_saving stage 2/3 (catalog_v4 ee_ttbar_nlo, V/B, m_t 172.5, catalog val, searched 8-trial DyHPO per (D, arm), stage2_readout.py at 0d5ce5fc): the same question on catalog data with a trees-in parent; this design differs in the data (KIT's m_t 173, mu_R = sqrt s, bulk beta 0.2-0.98), the parent (fair_nlo: 10 one-loop pools, Bakar's cap) and the readout (KIT bins, evaluate.py). Entry findings: protocol A at 1e5/9e5 (V target, not V/B) Coulomb bin 7-8.7 log10-MSE, B 2.38; no V/B run on KIT yet. results.tex: no KIT fair NLO result (searched fair_nlo, Bakar, V/B KIT)." \
 --measure "Per D and arm, the best trial (lowest val mu MSE, bulk-only validation) scored by tools/kit_predict.py with KIT's evaluate.py: bulk_test log10-MSE, every hard_test stratum's log10-MSE, bias, 99th percentile, |M|^2-weighted error, the fitted threshold and Sudakov exponents; curves of each against D for both arms (figure kit_fairnlo_<measure>), and the D ratio at equal bulk error where the curves overlap (as pretrain_data_saving)." \
 --check "The V/B path is new on KIT pools (a Born sidecar written from the file's born for the same events, kit_predict reads it): D395 smoke run, one trial-sized run per arm at D=1e2 for ~50 steps through training, sigma stage and KIT scoring, before the searches. The measure moves with pretraining on this target's catalog twin: pretrain_data_saving's ee_ttbar_nlo fine-tunes vs scratch (stage-2 readout). Lorentz invariance and float64 path tested (tests/test_input_reps.py, tests/test_kit_hardps.py)." \
 --fixed "KIT kit_ee_tt__virt_finite, train = the first D events of bulk_train, val = the last 1e5 of bulk_train (bulk-only early stopping), test bulk_test + every hard_test stratum; float64; the fair_nlo parent's config.yaml as base (model, inputs: no input flags, as the parent); V/B with physics factors off (as gen_data_saving VB); T(D) = the ee_ttbar_nlo horizons of pretrain_data_saving (D391: 5950 steps at 1e2, 8500 at 3.2e2..1e4); 8-trial single-fidelity DyHPO per (D, arm) over the template space (scratch: lr in [c/3, 3c] around the calibration's law; fine-tune: lr_scale [0.1, 10], layer_decay [0.75, 1], target stats own, off-shellness stats own), waves 3,3,2; HETEROSC mu_mse selection then the sigma stage; seed 42. 10 searches, 80 trials." \
 --control "Bakar's baseline: from-scratch V/B with the exact Born at the same D, searched the same way (8 trials); Bakar's MLP numbers from KIT's README as the external reference." \
 --seeds "One seed per trial (D315); each arm's value is its best of 8 trials, as the data-saving study; a difference inside 0.3 decades (2.5-3.7x the 0.08-0.12 seed spread at results.tex l.1294-1299) is unresolved." \
 --outcome "Per D: fine-tune better (bulk and the strata, median log10 ratio below -0.3), equal or worse. Yes (pretraining saves one-loop data on KIT): the fine-tune's bulk curve lies below the baseline's at every D with a D ratio > 1 at equal error, reported with the per-bin picture (Coulomb, Sudakov) per D. No: the baseline matches or beats it at D >= 1e3; then the fair NLO table goes to KIT as is and the draft's NLO transfer claim is restricted to the catalog setting. Mixed: per D and family." 2>&1 | tail -2
